.TH "GIT\-DELETE\-TAG" "1" "October 2017" "" "Git Extras"
.
.SH "NAME"
\fBgit\-delete\-tag\fR \- Delete tags
.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBgit delete\-tag\fR [\-h|\-\-help] <tagname>...
.
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Deletes local and remote tag named <tagname>\.
.
.SH "OPTIONS"
\-h, \-\-help
.P
Show help message and exit\.
.P
<tagname>
.
.P
The name of the tag to delete\. If multiple tags are provided, then they will all be deleted\.
.
.SH "DIAGNOSTICS"
If no tag name is supplied, \fBgit delete\-tag\fR exits with status 1 and explains that a tag name is required\.
If local tag deletion fails, it exits with status 1 and suggests inspecting tags using \fBgit tag \-l\fR\.
If remote tag deletion fails, it reports a troubleshooting hint to verify remote connectivity and permissions\.
.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.
.nf

$ git delete\-tag 0\.0\.1
$ git delete\-tag 0\.0\.1 0\.0\.2
.
.fi
.
